  "notes": {
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b003:l004": "Себилдүүсү is rendered as armed men; the line's number eighty-four is preserved.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b003:l010": "Бил мүчөлүү is rendered as elephant-limbed, using the primary Yudakhin бил elephant sense.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b003:l011": "Комокойлуу describes the socket or throat of the patterned spear; broad-socketed is contextual and uncertain.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b005:l008": "Burut is retained as the historical exonym for the Kyrgyz in the hostile speaker's dream account.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b005:l024": "Майлаган буудай describes an oiled-wheat complexion or sheen; rendered literally as a face like oiled wheat.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0004:b005:l039": "Ыстам дини is rendered as the faith of Islam, following the established normalized religious term."
